        "promptSimple":  "Use my image and fix the exposure: brighten the underexposed areas, recover the detail hidden in the shadows, and balance the contrast and highlights so the image looks correctly lit. Keep the composition, subject, colors, and mood exactly the same.",
        "promptExtended":  "Use the provided image and preserve the original composition, character identity, clothing, lighting direction, color palette character, lens perspective, and environment layout. This is a still-image transformation producing a single corrected photograph.\nCorrect the lighting of the underexposed photograph: lift the overall brightness to a natural, correctly exposed level, recover the detail buried in the dark areas — faces, clothing folds, interior surfaces, background elements — and balance the contrast so blacks stay rich without being crushed and highlights stay bright without clipping. Midtones open up so the subject reads clearly, while the original direction of light, the mood of the scene, and the color character are faithfully kept; a moody scene stays moody, just properly readable. Skin tones become natural and true, and previously invisible parts of the environment emerge cleanly from the shadows. The result looks like the same photograph exposed correctly in camera. No changes to the subject, no face morphing, no background redesign, no added or removed objects, no color-grade restyling."
